    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Chronic myeloid leukaemia (CML)",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Splenomegaly is a common finding in CML. The spleen is enlarged, with a uniform dark-red appearance and a fine nodular pattern of retained white pulp areas (&lt;&lt;39597&gt;&gt;). Granulocytes, eosinophils, and small hypolobulated megakaryocytes can be appreciated in dilated splenic sinuses (&lt;&lt;39598&gt;&gt;).",
